---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { Mail } from "@lucide/astro";
import GithubIcon from "../components/ui/icons/GithubIcon.astro";
import LinkedinIcon from "../components/ui/icons/LinkedinIcon.astro";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/seo";
import { getPublishedPosts, typeLabel } from "../lib/collections";
import portrait from "../assets/arun.png";

const links = [
  { label: "GitHub", href: SITE.github, Icon: GithubIcon },
  { label: "LinkedIn", href: SITE.linkedin, Icon: LinkedinIcon },
  { label: "Email", href: `mailto:${SITE.email}`, Icon: Mail },
];

// Evidence for the research interests: typed posts first, newest first.
const EVIDENCE_TYPES = ["experiment", "benchmark", "reproduction", "ablation", "explainer", "buildlog"];
const evidence = (await getPublishedPosts())
  .filter((p) => EVIDENCE_TYPES.includes(p.data.type))
  .slice(0, 6);
---

<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="Arun MV, an AI engineer who builds production LLM systems and studies why they fail: retrieval, LLM evaluation and agent reliability."
  prose
>
  <div class="flex flex-col-reverse gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
      I build production LLM systems and study why they fail.
    </h1>
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Arun MV"
      width={320}
      height={320}
      class="h-28 w-28 shrink-0 rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-border object-cover shadow-sm sm:h-40 sm:w-40"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>Hey, I'm Arun.</p>
    <p>
      I'm an AI engineer. Most of my work has been shipping LLM systems that people depend on:
      retrieval pipelines, agents, and the evals and cost controls around them. That work is where
      my research questions come from. A system passes its evals and still fails a user. A
      retrieval stack scores well on average and misses exactly the question that mattered. An
      agent does the right thing for the wrong reason.
    </p>
    <p>
      There's more AI-generated writing than ever, and most of it says nothing. I try to do the
      opposite: publish less, measure more, and only put something out when there's a number, a
      mechanism or a working artifact behind it.
    </p>

    <h2>Research interests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Retrieval over structured knowledge.</strong> When relationship-aware retrieval
        (graphs, entity links, multi-hop) beats flat hybrid search, and what it costs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Evaluation methodology for LLM systems.</strong> Judge calibration, noise floors and
        minimum detectable effects, and whether an eval suite can see the regression you care about.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Agent reliability.</strong> Bounded agents, tool-use failures, and checking the path
        an agent took as well as its outcome.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>I write the hypothesis down, with a date, before I run the experiment.</li>
      <li>Every number I publish carries its sample size, seeds or a confidence interval.</li>
      <li>Null and negative results get published as findings.</li>
      <li>Code, configs and a one-command rerun go up with the write-up when the data allows it.</li>
    </ul>

    {
      evidence.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <h2>Selected writing</h2>
          <ul>
            {evidence.map((p) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`/blog/${p.id}`}>{p.data.title}</a>{" "}
                <span class="font-mono text-sm text-faint">· {typeLabel(p.data.type)}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2>Outside work</h2>
    <p>
      Football, mostly. I follow it too closely. I also write the occasional personal essay; those
      live in their own stream and never mix with the technical feed.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you work on retrieval, evals or agent reliability and want to compare notes, or you're
      hiring for research roles in this area, email me.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 flex gap-4">
    {
      links.map(({ label, href, Icon }) => (
        <a
          href={href}
          aria-label={label}
          target={href.startsWith("mailto") ? undefined : "_blank"}
          rel="me noopener"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-[var(--radius-md)] border border-border px-3 py-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"
        >
          <Icon size={16} stroke-width={1.5} /> {label}
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</PageLayout>
